  "authoringNote": "Partial S3 snapshot (D5 reverse access) with the recorded conservative limitation; this is not completed F13 recovery. f13x5-order v1 has case-scoped metadata and is restricted (null contentHash, no payload). v2 is a valid final order with trusted supersedes {f13x5-order, 1}; the receipt links v2. v1 is superseded, not current and not a C09 candidate, so R03 and R04 have no restricted condition and pass on v2. R09 still classifies every supplied version that metadata quarantine does not exclude: R09 is restricted for the authorization_coordinator with R09.access_restricted naming f13x5-order v1 (needs_information), parent [f13x5-order v1]. State needs_information. R01 to R05 pass on v2 with the standard citation sets (8, 6, 9, 6, 4). R06 is manual_review for the qualified_clinical_reviewer with R06.clinical_review (no refs, effect none) and cites the five /clinical/ statements of the usable encounter; R07 passes citing /lcmpReport/incorporated (false; the null evaluationDate is not cited); R08 passes; R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. Every other parent is empty. Superseded [f13x5-order v1]; quarantine empty. Recorded reading: a rule cites evidence-field facts only from the documents it reads, and R04 reads only final current usable records; every usable encounter and order here is final, so no draft is excluded. The standard chronology holds: the order date 2026-09-08 is after the 2026-08-24 encounter (not the same day, so C02 does not apply) and inside the C01 bound 2027-02-24, and the receipt at 2026-09-09T16:30:00Z is after the C06 span of the order date, which ends 2026-09-09T12:00Z. Deferred to S4: the disposition of superseded unusable versions, arrival-order recovery, history display, replay and rollback prevention.",
